From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250: set the SLPI FastRPC heap VMID

The Pocket 5 IMU is an ICM-4x6xx behind the SLPI. This kernel assigns an
SDSP memory-region to the sensors VM during FastRPC probe, and that call
fails on the Pocket 5, so the fastrpc-sdsp device never appears. Leave
the region out. The VMID is enough: the sensors PD allocates a heap when
it attaches and assigns that buffer itself.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
@@ -3121,6 +3121,8 @@
 					compatible = "qcom,fastrpc";
 					qcom,glink-channels = "fastrpcglink-apps-dsp";
 					label = "sdsp";
+					/* SSC_Q6. No memory-region: probe assigns that immediately. */
+					qcom,vmids = <0x5>;
 					qcom,non-secure-domain;
 					#address-cells = <1>;
 					#size-cells = <0>;
